    "One small panel and one realization per arm; paired tasks do not remove service/model variability. No universal speedup or accuracy gain is established.",
    "All twelve public task groups are fresh versus previous panels; four authored negative controls are deliberately reused and not independent new negatives.",
    "V1/V2 are development evidence. V3 uses expected seconds for joint resource allocation/admission/generation caps; empirical upper seconds are diagnostic. Historical priors, token reservations and absolute SDK/local deadlines remain unchanged.",
    "Only90-second comparisons are repeated on this image. Full3300-second v1 observations remain historical; they are not measurements of this new image.",
    "On-time scores use recorded agent-relative answer emission times. Container wall time additionally includes startup and shutdown; relay drain is separate.",
    "Provider usage after a local timeout remains charged. Local reservation holds are not extra provider charges or measured-zero calls.",
    "Time-MAE/upper coverage use completed, known, non-deadline-limited attempts. Cohorts differ across arms; their MAEs are not paired accuracy comparisons.",
    "Empirical upper coverage is descriptive, not a guarantee. Historical priors are unchanged and use old public100, excluding final20 and all SLA panels.",
    "Expected seconds is the runtime scheduling point-estimate name, not a demonstrated calibrated conditional mean; no constants were fitted to this retest.",
    "Search grading uses exact accepted spans; a longer factually correct span can be a grading mismatch.",
    "Queue-pressure counts describe selected trace visits, not every rejected scheduler candidate."
